  "problem": "A primary school teacher records how many words his second-year students can read in 5 minutes. The number of words read is distributed with a population standard deviation of $\\sigma =36$ words. In a school of $180$ students, he finds that the mean number of read words is $255$ words. Find a $95%$ confidence interval for the mean number of words $\\mu $ for the entire population of second-year children.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ the table below shows the $z$-scores ${z}_{p}$ such that $P(Z>{z}_{p})=p$ for some particular values of $p.$*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${z}_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |",
